<% content_for :title, "GEO by Mod Op" %>
<div id="container" class="case case--geo">
    <%= render "home/case_header" %>
    <p class="crumb case-wayfinding">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span aria-current="page">Case study</span>
    </p>

    <section id="cs-top">
        <h1>GEO by Mod Op</h1>
        <h2>A live product that shows brands how they appear in AI answers, with a free audit that leads into an ongoing optimization program. It went live in June 2026, Mod Op launched it publicly in August 2026, and it runs at <a href="https://geo.modop.ai" target="_blank">geo.modop.ai</a>.</h2>
        <figure class="story-illustration case-header-visual">
            <%= image_tag "geo-header-scan.jpg", alt: "Hand-drawn person scanning a landscape of changing signals with a magnifying glass" %>
        </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-situation">
        <h3>The gap</h3>
        <p>People were asking ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity for recommendations and explanations alongside their Google searches. A brand could perform well in search and have little presence in those answers. Search rankings gave one view of a brand. AI answers gave another. The first question for GEO was simple: how could a brand see its position from a buyer's point of view? The second was practical: a website is a structured source that AI systems read and cite, so an agent could audit one against the criteria that matter.</p>
        <p>Our search and strategy experts already had a useful manual audit, but it took weeks to assemble and was usually a one-off. The first GEO prototype was built in about four hours during the February 2026 <a href="/launchpad">Launchpad</a> hackathon. It drew strong feedback from staff in the prototype directory, and it was one of three working prototypes we put in front of a beverage client that spring. Between that internal signal and what we were hearing from clients about the problems they wanted help with, we promoted GEO and wrote its MVP spec. Audience Lab was the first Launchpad concept to reach a live MVP. GEO followed a few weeks later. The job was to turn that audit into a repeatable product that someone outside the agency could understand quickly and choose to continue.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-role">
        <h3>What I owned</h3>
        <p>I took GEO from a hackathon prototype through scope, engineering design, and MVP into a live product in about four months. I directed the design and build, worked with Mod Op's search and strategy experts to turn their manual audit into a repeatable experience, defined the reporting and scoring framework with them, and connected the free audit to the paid program. I stayed involved through stakeholder alignment, go-to-market, and the June 2026 launch.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-audit">
        <h3>The product decision</h3>
        <figure class="geo-walkthrough">
            <button type="button" class="geo-pip-trigger" data-geo-pip-trigger data-video-src="/geo-homepage-walkthrough.mp4" data-video-poster="<%= image_path("geo-homepage-first-frame.jpg") %>" data-video-title="GEO Landing Page Demo" aria-controls="geo-pip" aria-label="Play the GEO Landing Page Demo video">
                <%= image_tag "geo-homepage-first-frame.jpg", alt: "" %>
                <span class="geo-pip-trigger__play" aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
            </button>
        </figure>
        <p>The free audit begins with brand and category research, then tests the questions buyers are likely to ask across ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity. The report shows where the brand appears, how often it is cited, and how it compares with named competitors.</p>
        <p>The interface was designed in Claude Design with the Mod Op brand skill enabled, the same style guide I had written as an agent skill during the hackathon, so the product looked like Mod Op from its first screen.</p>
        <p>The score is a starting point. The useful part is the evidence behind it: the prompts a brand appears for, the questions it is missing, the competitors winning attention, and the citations each engine returns. That gives a team something concrete to discuss and a clearer view of where the brand can improve.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-framework">
        <h3>The framework</h3>
        <figure class="geo-results-walkthrough">
            <button type="button" class="geo-pip-trigger geo-pip-trigger--results" data-geo-pip-trigger data-geo-pip-audit-trigger data-video-src="/geo-audit-results-walkthrough-table-dwells-1s-longer.mp4" data-video-poster="<%= image_path("geo-audit-results-first-frame.jpg") %>" data-video-title="Free GEO Audit Results Demo" aria-controls="geo-pip" aria-label="Play the Free GEO Audit Results Demo video">
                <%= image_tag "geo-audit-results-first-frame.jpg", alt: "" %>
                <span class="geo-pip-trigger__play" aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
            </button>
        </figure>
        <p>The GEO Periodic Table organizes 25 factors into a practical review of content quality, structured data, brand and entity signals, trustworthiness, performance, and engagement. Each factor points to work a team can take on.</p>
        <p>The audit works through those factors in an agentic sequence of research, prompt testing, comparison, and synthesis. The results page makes that depth legible: a team can see how each factor was assessed, understand where the brand stands, and see which changes are likely to matter first.</p>
        <p>The report becomes a clear handoff from diagnosis to a conversation about what to do next.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-funnel">
        <h3>From audit to program</h3>
        <p>We designed the free audit to be useful on its own. From there, the paid program offers a deeper baseline, a cross-channel plan, and ongoing measurement for teams that want help improving the result. The handoff had to feel like the next useful step in the same conversation.</p>
        <p>The audit went live on June 18, 2026. Eight weeks later, Mod Op launched it publicly and used it to publish the GEO 50, a ranking of 50 major brands across eight categories. I had left by then and was not part of the benchmark. The company kept shipping on the system we built.</p>
        <figure class="story-illustration">
            <%= image_tag "geo-cultivated-signal.jpg", alt: "Hand-drawn person tending a growing tree of signals and ideas" %>
        </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-learned">
        <h3>What I learned</h3>
        <p>We spent a lot of time deciding how much the audit should give away. The answer turned out more generous than I first expected. If someone could leave with a clear understanding of their position, they had a reason to trust the paid program. The audit became the first step in the relationship, and the paid program had a clear job: help the team act on what it had learned.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-sources">
        <h3>Links</h3>
        <ul class="source-list">
            <li>
                <a href="https://geo.modop.ai" target="_blank">GEO</a>
                <span class="source-list__detail">geo.modop.ai · live service and free audit application.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://www.modop.com/press/mod-op-launches-free-ai-search-visibility-tool-and-unveils-the-geo-50/" target="_blank">Mod Op Launches Free AI Search Visibility Tool and Unveils the GEO 50</a>
                <span class="source-list__detail">Mod Op press release · August 2026 launch announcement.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://digiday.com/marketing/build-or-buy-inside-indie-agency-mod-ops-ai-infrastructure/" target="_blank">Build or Buy? Inside Indie Agency Mod Op’s AI Infrastructure</a>
                <span class="source-list__detail">Digiday · August 2026 coverage of the broader AI platform.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="crumb case-back-home"><a href="/">&larr; Back home</a></p>
    <%= render "home/case_footer" %>
</div>

<div id="geo-pip-backdrop" class="geo-pip-backdrop" data-geo-pip-backdrop hidden aria-hidden="true"></div>

<div id="geo-pip" class="geo-pip" data-geo-pip data-corner="bottom-right" data-size="small" aria-label="GEO video player, small size">
    <div class="geo-pip__bar" data-geo-pip-drag-handle title="Drag to move the video">
        <span class="geo-pip__title" data-geo-pip-title>GEO Landing Page Demo</span>
        <div class="geo-pip__controls" aria-label="Video size controls">
            <button type="button" class="geo-pip__size geo-pip__minus" data-geo-pip-minus aria-label="Make video smaller" title="Make video smaller">−</button>
            <button type="button" class="geo-pip__size geo-pip__plus" data-geo-pip-plus aria-label="Make video larger" title="Make video larger">+</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="geo-pip__stage">
        <video id="geo-pip-video" class="geo-pip__player" autoplay loop muted playsinline preload="auto" tabindex="0" src="/geo-homepage-walkthrough.mp4" poster="<%= image_path("geo-homepage-first-frame.jpg") %>" aria-label="GEO Landing Page Demo. Click to pause or resume."></video>
        <span class="geo-pip__feedback" data-geo-pip-feedback aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    (() => {
        const pip = document.querySelector("[data-geo-pip]");
        const backdrop = document.querySelector("[data-geo-pip-backdrop]");
        const video = document.querySelector("#geo-pip-video");
        const title = pip && pip.querySelector("[data-geo-pip-title]");
        const triggers = document.querySelectorAll("[data-geo-pip-trigger]");
        const auditTrigger = document.querySelector("[data-geo-pip-audit-trigger]");
        const plus = pip && pip.querySelector("[data-geo-pip-plus]");
        const minus = pip && pip.querySelector("[data-geo-pip-minus]");
        const dragHandle = pip && pip.querySelector("[data-geo-pip-drag-handle]");
        const feedback = pip && pip.querySelector("[data-geo-pip-feedback]");

        if (!pip || !backdrop || !video || !title || !plus || !minus || !dragHandle || !feedback) return;

        let activeCorner = pip.dataset.corner || "bottom-right";
        let sizeStage = 1;
        let dragState = null;
        let backdropTimer = null;
        let backdropFrame = null;
        let auditTransitionPending = false;
        let auditTransitioned = false;
        let feedbackAnimation = null;

        const clearSnapAnimation = () => {
            pip.classList.remove("geo-pip--snap-start", "geo-pip--snap-end");
            pip.style.removeProperty("--pip-snap-x");
            pip.style.removeProperty("--pip-snap-y");
            pip.style.removeProperty("transform");
        };

        const clearPositionStyles = () => {
            pip.style.removeProperty("left");
            pip.style.removeProperty("top");
            pip.style.removeProperty("right");
            pip.style.removeProperty("bottom");
        };

        const setCorner = (corner) => {
            activeCorner = corner;
            pip.dataset.corner = corner;
        };

        const container = document.querySelector(".case--geo");
        const reserveSpace = () => {
            if (!container) return;
            const reserve = (pip.hidden || sizeStage === 3) ? 0 : pip.offsetHeight + 24;
            container.style.setProperty("--geo-pip-reserve", `${reserve}px`);
        };

        const updateSizeControls = () => {
            const size = ["minimal", "small", "medium", "big"][sizeStage];
            const minusLabels = [
                ["Video is at minimum size", "Video is at minimum size"],
                ["Minimize video", "Minimize video"],
                ["Make video smaller", "Make video smaller"],
                ["Make video medium", "Make video medium"]
            ];
            const plusLabels = [
                ["Show video", "Show video"],
                ["Make video medium", "Make video medium"],
                ["Make video big", "Make video big"],
                ["Video is at maximum size", "Video is at maximum size"]
            ];
            const [minusLabel, minusTitle] = minusLabels[sizeStage];
            const [plusLabel, plusTitle] = plusLabels[sizeStage];

            pip.dataset.size = size;
            pip.classList.toggle("geo-pip--minimal", sizeStage === 0);
            pip.classList.toggle("geo-pip--medium", sizeStage === 2);
            pip.classList.toggle("geo-pip--big", sizeStage === 3);

            minus.disabled = sizeStage === 0;
            plus.disabled = sizeStage === 3;
            minus.setAttribute("aria-label", minusLabel);
            minus.title = minusTitle;
            plus.setAttribute("aria-label", plusLabel);
            plus.title = plusTitle;
            pip.setAttribute("aria-label", `GEO video player, ${size} size`);
            reserveSpace();
            window.setTimeout(reserveSpace, 320);
        };

        const snapToCorner = (corner, animate = true) => {
            const fromRect = pip.getBoundingClientRect();
            clearSnapAnimation();
            clearPositionStyles();
            setCorner(corner);

            if (!animate || !fromRect.width) return;

            const toRect = pip.getBoundingClientRect();
            const offsetX = fromRect.left - toRect.left;
            const offsetY = fromRect.top - toRect.top;
            if (Math.abs(offsetX) < 1 && Math.abs(offsetY) < 1) return;

            pip.style.setProperty("--pip-snap-x", `${offsetX}px`);
            pip.style.setProperty("--pip-snap-y", `${offsetY}px`);
            pip.classList.add("geo-pip--snap-start");
            pip.offsetWidth;
            requestAnimationFrame(() => pip.classList.add("geo-pip--snap-end"));

            window.setTimeout(clearSnapAnimation, 320);
        };

        const nearestCorner = (rect) => {
            const margin = window.innerWidth <= 900 ? 12 : 16;
            const maxLeft = Math.max(margin, window.innerWidth - rect.width - margin);
            const maxTop = Math.max(margin, window.innerHeight - rect.height - margin);
            const points = {
                "top-left": { left: margin, top: margin },
                "top-right": { left: maxLeft, top: margin },
                "bottom-left": { left: margin, top: maxTop },
                "bottom-right": { left: maxLeft, top: maxTop }
            };

            return Object.entries(points).reduce((closest, [corner, point]) => {
                const distance = Math.hypot(rect.left - point.left, rect.top - point.top);
                return distance < closest.distance ? { corner, distance } : closest;
            }, { corner: activeCorner, distance: Infinity }).corner;
        };

        const playVideo = () => {
            video.muted = true;
            const playback = video.play();
            if (playback && typeof playback.catch === "function") playback.catch(() => {});
        };

        const selectVideo = (trigger, shouldPlay = true) => {
            const src = trigger.dataset.videoSrc;
            if (!src) return;

            const sourceChanged = video.dataset.source !== src;
            title.textContent = trigger.dataset.videoTitle || "GEO Landing Page Demo";
            video.setAttribute("aria-label", `${trigger.dataset.videoTitle || "GEO Landing Page Demo"}. Click to pause or resume.`);
            pip.hidden = false;
            if (auditTrigger && src === auditTrigger.dataset.videoSrc) auditTransitioned = true;

            if (sourceChanged) {
                video.pause();
                video.src = src;
                video.dataset.source = src;
                if (trigger.dataset.videoPoster) {
                    video.poster = trigger.dataset.videoPoster;
                } else {
                    video.removeAttribute("poster");
                }
                video.load();
            }

            if (video.ended) video.currentTime = 0;
            if (sizeStage !== 0 && shouldPlay) playVideo();
        };

        const showBackdrop = () => {
            window.clearTimeout(backdropTimer);
            window.cancelAnimationFrame(backdropFrame);
            backdrop.hidden = false;
            backdropFrame = window.requestAnimationFrame(() => backdrop.classList.add("geo-pip-backdrop--visible"));
        };

        const hideBackdrop = () => {
            window.cancelAnimationFrame(backdropFrame);
            backdrop.classList.remove("geo-pip-backdrop--visible");
            window.clearTimeout(backdropTimer);
            backdropTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
                backdrop.hidden = true;
            }, 240);
        };

        const setSize = (nextStage) => {
            if (nextStage < 0 || nextStage > 3 || nextStage === sizeStage) return;
            const wasPlaying = !video.paused;
            const wasMinimal = sizeStage === 0;

            if (nextStage === 3) {
                clearSnapAnimation();
                const rect = pip.getBoundingClientRect();
                pip.style.left = `${rect.left + rect.width / 2}px`;
                pip.style.top = `${rect.top + rect.height / 2}px`;
                pip.style.right = "auto";
                pip.style.bottom = "auto";
                sizeStage = nextStage;
                updateSizeControls();
                document.body.classList.add("geo-pip-focus-lock");
                showBackdrop();
                window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {
                    pip.style.left = "50%";
                    pip.style.top = "50%";
                });
            } else if (sizeStage === 3) {
                const rect = pip.getBoundingClientRect();
                clearSnapAnimation();
                pip.style.left = `${rect.left}px`;
                pip.style.top = `${rect.top}px`;
                pip.style.right = "auto";
                pip.style.bottom = "auto";
                sizeStage = nextStage;
                updateSizeControls();
                document.body.classList.remove("geo-pip-focus-lock");
                hideBackdrop();
                window.requestAnimationFrame(() => snapToCorner(activeCorner));
            } else {
                clearSnapAnimation();
                sizeStage = nextStage;
                updateSizeControls();
            }

            if (sizeStage === 0) {
                video.pause();
            } else if (wasPlaying || wasMinimal) {
                playVideo();
            }
        };

        const transitionToAuditVideo = async () => {
            if (!auditTrigger || auditTransitionPending || auditTransitioned) return;

            const auditSrc = auditTrigger.dataset.videoSrc;
            if (!auditSrc || video.dataset.source === auditSrc) {
                auditTransitioned = true;
                return;
            }

            auditTransitionPending = true;
            auditTransitioned = true;
            const shouldPlay = !video.paused;
            clearSnapAnimation();

            const rect = pip.getBoundingClientRect();
            const isLeft = activeCorner === "top-left" || activeCorner === "bottom-left" ||
                (activeCorner !== "top-right" && activeCorner !== "bottom-right" && rect.left + rect.width / 2 < window.innerWidth / 2);
            const distance = isLeft ? -(rect.right + 48) : window.innerWidth - rect.left + 48;

            pip.style.setProperty("--pip-transition-x", `${distance}px`);
            pip.classList.add("geo-pip--transitioning-out");

            await new Promise((resolve) => window.setTimeout(resolve, 400));
            selectVideo(auditTrigger, shouldPlay);
            pip.classList.remove("geo-pip--transitioning-out");
            pip.style.removeProperty("--pip-transition-x");
            auditTransitionPending = false;
        };

        triggers.forEach((trigger) => {
            trigger.addEventListener("click", () => {
                const wasMinimized = sizeStage === 0;
                selectVideo(trigger, !wasMinimized);
                if (wasMinimized) setSize(1);
            });
        });

        plus.addEventListener("click", () => {
            if (sizeStage < 3) setSize(sizeStage + 1);
        });

        minus.addEventListener("click", () => {
            if (sizeStage > 0) setSize(sizeStage - 1);
        });

        backdrop.addEventListener("click", () => setSize(2));

        const handleScroll = () => {
            const scrollableHeight = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
            if (scrollableHeight > 0 && window.scrollY >= scrollableHeight * 0.5) {
                transitionToAuditVideo();
            }
        };

        window.addEventListener("scroll", handleScroll, { passive: true });

        dragHandle.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
            const target = event.target;
            if ((target instanceof Element && target.closest("button")) || event.button === 2 || sizeStage === 3) return;

            const rect = pip.getBoundingClientRect();
            dragState = {
                pointerId: event.pointerId,
                startX: event.clientX,
                startY: event.clientY,
                left: rect.left,
                top: rect.top,
                width: rect.width,
                height: rect.height
            };
            clearSnapAnimation();
            pip.classList.add("geo-pip--dragging");
            pip.dataset.corner = "dragging";
            pip.style.left = `${rect.left}px`;
            pip.style.top = `${rect.top}px`;
            pip.style.right = "auto";
            pip.style.bottom = "auto";
            if (dragHandle.setPointerCapture) dragHandle.setPointerCapture(event.pointerId);
            event.preventDefault();
        });

        dragHandle.addEventListener("pointermove", (event) => {
            if (!dragState || event.pointerId !== dragState.pointerId) return;

            const margin = window.innerWidth <= 900 ? 12 : 16;
            const maxLeft = Math.max(margin, window.innerWidth - dragState.width - margin);
            const maxTop = Math.max(margin, window.innerHeight - dragState.height - margin);
            const left = Math.min(maxLeft, Math.max(margin, dragState.left + event.clientX - dragState.startX));
            const top = Math.min(maxTop, Math.max(margin, dragState.top + event.clientY - dragState.startY));
            pip.style.left = `${left}px`;
            pip.style.top = `${top}px`;
        });

        const finishDrag = (event) => {
            if (!dragState || event.pointerId !== dragState.pointerId) return;
            if (dragHandle.hasPointerCapture && dragHandle.hasPointerCapture(event.pointerId)) dragHandle.releasePointerCapture(event.pointerId);
            dragState = null;
            pip.classList.remove("geo-pip--dragging");
            snapToCorner(nearestCorner(pip.getBoundingClientRect()));
        };

        dragHandle.addEventListener("pointerup", finishDrag);
        dragHandle.addEventListener("pointercancel", finishDrag);

        document.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
            if (event.key !== "Escape" || pip.hidden) return;
            if (sizeStage === 3) setSize(2);
            else if (sizeStage > 0) setSize(0);
        });

        window.addEventListener("resize", reserveSpace);
        video.addEventListener("loadedmetadata", reserveSpace);
        setCorner(activeCorner);
        updateSizeControls();
        video.dataset.source = video.currentSrc || video.src;
        playVideo();
        window.requestAnimationFrame(handleScroll);

        const showPlaybackFeedback = (icon) => {
            feedback.textContent = icon;
            feedback.dataset.icon = icon === "▶" ? "play" : "pause";
            if (feedbackAnimation) feedbackAnimation.cancel();
            feedbackAnimation = feedback.animate([
                {
                    opacity: 0.9,
                    transform: "translate3d(-50%, -50%, 0) scale(1)"
                },
                {
                    offset: 0.36,
                    opacity: 0.84,
                    transform: "translate3d(-50%, -50%, 0) scale(1.1)"
                },
                {
                    offset: 0.68,
                    opacity: 0.52,
                    transform: "translate3d(-50%, -50%, 0) scale(1.3)"
                },
                {
                    opacity: 0,
                    transform: "translate3d(-50%, -50%, 0) scale(1.58)"
                }
            ], {
                duration: 480,
                easing: "cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)",
                fill: "both"
            });
            feedbackAnimation.onfinish = () => {
                feedbackAnimation = null;
            };
        };

        const togglePlayback = () => {
            const isPaused = video.paused;
            if (isPaused) playVideo();
            else video.pause();

            showPlaybackFeedback(isPaused ? "▶" : "⏸");
        };

        video.addEventListener("click", togglePlayback);
        video.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
            if (event.key !== " " && event.key !== "Enter") return;
            event.preventDefault();
            togglePlayback();
        });
    })();
</script>
